(6008975, 880518, 61396, '<td valign="top">For me - you created a world (the glass, the dust, the sideway look, the eyes, the tears like stains, the pressed hand) I can look at, yet never be able to fully comprehend - a frozen illustration of another soul. Inspiring.<br/> <br/>Coming back to say that I see the glass playing a double role of both separation (of the figure from the world) and yet it also provides and enhances meaning (e.g. the dust suggesting something from the past, the stains hinting at tears, or maybe bubbles as the background can be deep water).<br/> <br/>Coming back again to see if the magic has gone. It has not.</td>', 'For me - you created a world (the glass, the dust, the sideway look, the eyes, the tears like stains, the pressed hand) I can look at, yet never be able to fully comprehend - a frozen illustration of another soul. Inspiring. Coming back to say that I see the glass playing a double role of both separation (of the figure from the world) and yet it also provides and enhances meaning (e.g. the dust suggesting something from the past, the stains hinting at tears, or maybe bubbles as the background can be deep water). Coming back again to see if the magic has gone. It has not.', '2010-05-16 06:58:39.000000', NULL, 1),
