(6023036, 879212, 66709, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JH:</b></div><hr/><i> There''s something quite surreal about this shot that I enjoy - the pin-sharp background and OOF subject; honestly - how difficult is that to achieve given the auto-focus mechanisms in most dSLRs? It almost looks like bear was a cut/paste onto that background.<br/> <br/>Anyway, this was the only shot in this challenge that stuck in my head - I was looking forward to seeing if you''d achieved another brown ribbon. :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>one contest too early</td>', 'Originally posted by JH: There''s something quite surreal about this shot that I enjoy - the pin-sharp background and OOF subject; honestly - how difficult is that to achieve given the auto-focus mechanisms in most dSLRs? It almost looks like bear was a cut/paste onto that background. Anyway, this was the only shot in this challenge that stuck in my head - I was looking forward to seeing if you''d achieved another brown ribbon. :)   one contest too early', '2010-05-24 00:32:11.000000', NULL, 0),
